# ==============================================================
# OCEAN PUZZLE - INSTRUCTIONS: ROOM 3 (Symbol Values)
# ==============================================================
# Script type : interact
# Bind to     : [FILL IN: x y z of the clickable head block]
# Map/area    : [FILL IN: map name / room]
# Import      : /s i i <paste URL>, then click the head block
#
# What it does:
#   The Oracle explains the symbol value grid puzzle.
#   Can be replayed once every 45 seconds per player.
#
# Requires: puzzle1 namespace (see Submit script header)
#
# Related scripts: Instructions Rooms 1-2 and 4 (share the same cooldown)
# ==============================================================
@using puzzle1
@define Long now = system::currentTimeMillis()

@if oracle_ready_at > now
    @define Long seconds = (oracle_ready_at - now + 999L) / 1000L
    @player &cOracle: You must wait {{seconds}} seconds to hear the instructions again.
    @return
@fi

@var oracle_ready_at = now + 45000L

@player &3Oracle: &bYou have learned which tones answer to the symbols.
@delay 3s
@player &3Oracle: &bNow the third chamber asks a deeper question: what number sleeps within each sign?
@delay 3s
@player &3Oracle: &bFive grids lie before you, each more tangled than the last.
@delay 3s
@player &3Oracle: &bThey offer no plain sum, no guiding mark of arithmetic.
@delay 3s
@player &3Oracle: &bStudy how the signs stand together. Their kinship is the key.
@delay 3s
@player &3Oracle: &bBy patient thought, uncover the value of all ten.
@delay 3s
@player &3Oracle: &bDo not mistake a pattern for a law until every grid agrees.
